# Benchmark: game loop
# Workload: a 60-frame 2D entity simulation with movement, boundary collision,
# and entity distance checks. Measures arithmetic, property reads/writes,
# and condition evaluation in an interactive simulation loop.

a Point has
    x
    y
    vx
    vy

player is a Point with x 50, y 50, vx 2, vy 1
enemy is a Point with x 10, y 20, vx 3, vy 2

score is 0
collisions is 0
frames is 60

count from 1 to frames as frame
    px is x of player
    py is y of player
    pvx is vx of player
    pvy is vy of player

    px is px plus pvx
    py is py plus pvy

    if px is greater than 100
        px is 100
        vx of player is 0 minus pvx
    otherwise if px is less than 0
        px is 0
        vx of player is 0 minus pvx
    .
    if py is greater than 100
        py is 100
        vy of player is 0 minus pvy
    otherwise if py is less than 0
        py is 0
        vy of player is 0 minus pvy
    .
    x of player is px
    y of player is py

    ex is x of enemy
    ey is y of enemy
    evx is vx of enemy
    evy is vy of enemy

    ex is ex plus evx
    ey is ey plus evy

    if ex is greater than 100
        ex is 100
        vx of enemy is 0 minus evx
    otherwise if ex is less than 0
        ex is 0
        vx of enemy is 0 minus evx
    .
    if ey is greater than 100
        ey is 100
        vy of enemy is 0 minus evy
    otherwise if ey is less than 0
        ey is 0
        vy of enemy is 0 minus evy
    .
    x of enemy is ex
    y of enemy is ey

    dx is px minus ex
    dy is py minus ey
    if dx is less than 0
        dx is 0 minus dx
    .
    if dy is less than 0
        dy is 0 minus dy
    .
    dist is dx plus dy
    if dist is less than 15
        collisions is collisions plus 1
        score is score plus 10
    otherwise
        score is score plus 1
    .
.

say "game loop" frames "frames, score" score "collisions" collisions "player" x of player y of player
